WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.597 --> 00:00:16.240
Luke's trial went more smoothly after that.

2
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.742
Of course, the prosecutor was not happy.

3
00:00:23.666 --> 00:00:26.448
He objected loudly, but the judge shut him up.

4
00:00:27.228 --> 00:00:31.392
Bob got on the witness stand and told everyone what really happened.

5
00:00:33.308 --> 00:00:36.529
Luke, Boggs, and Mendoza had been looking for gold.

6
00:00:41.611 --> 00:00:45.793
One day, Luke came across a large rock that turned out to be gold.

7
00:00:46.573 --> 00:00:51.115
When he showed it to Boggs and Mendoza, they wanted the gold for themselves.

8
00:00:52.836 --> 00:00:56.657
The next day, Boggs accidentally dropped his hat in the well.

9
00:00:56.677 --> 00:00:59.999
"Let me down the well," he said to Luke.

10
00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:05.102
So Boggs climbed into the bucket while Luke held tightly to the rope.

11
00:01:07.103 --> 00:01:09.265
At that point Mendoza walked by.

12
00:01:09.285 --> 00:01:11.586
"Aha, this is my chance!"

13
00:01:12.287 --> 00:01:13.347
he said to himself.

14
00:01:14.108 --> 00:01:17.631
He pulled out a gun and crept quietly toward Luke.

15
00:01:18.431 --> 00:01:20.192
Bob tried to warn his master.

16
00:01:22.094 --> 00:01:26.257
But all Luke's attention was on watching Boggs and holding the rope tight.

17
00:01:28.198 --> 00:01:30.420
Mendoza got closer and closer.

18
00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:34.221
Bob barked and barked, but Luke didn't hear.

19
00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:37.082
Bob knew Luke's life was in danger!

20
00:01:37.742 --> 00:01:40.963
So he opened his jaw and bit down hard on Luke's leg.

21
00:01:41.803 --> 00:01:44.344
Luke shouted in pain and let go of the rope.

22
00:01:44.364 --> 00:01:45.644
"Bad dog!

23
00:01:46.164 --> 00:01:46.824
Bad dog!"

24
00:01:47.385 --> 00:01:48.485
Luke scolded Bob.

25
00:01:50.686 --> 00:01:52.426
Mendoza quickly hid his gun.

26
00:01:52.446 --> 00:01:53.846
"What happened?"

27
00:01:54.427 --> 00:01:55.527
he asked innocently.

28
00:01:56.247 --> 00:01:57.707
They both looked down the well.

29
00:01:58.108 --> 00:01:59.148
Boggs was gone.

30
00:02:00.124 --> 00:02:02.706
Luke was upset, but Mendoza was sly.

31
00:02:02.726 --> 00:02:09.150
"If you don't give me the gold," he said, "I will tell everyone that you killed Boggs on

32
00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:12.493
purpose." So Luke gave the gold to Mendoza.

33
00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.874
The courtroom was silent.

34
00:02:15.495 --> 00:02:17.496
Some people even began crying.

35
00:02:17.516 --> 00:02:21.299
"Poor Luke," they said, "it wasn't his fault!"

36
00:02:22.119 --> 00:02:24.581
Even the judge wiped a tear from his eye.

37
00:02:26.702 --> 00:02:29.024
The next day, Luke stood before the judge.

38
00:02:29.556 --> 00:02:32.037
"You are not guilty," he declared.

39
00:02:32.757 --> 00:02:34.918
Everyone jumped up and clapped loudly.

40
00:02:36.258 --> 00:02:38.659
Dr. Dolittle and Tommy ran up to Luke.

41
00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:44.640
He smiled at them and said simply, "Thank you."

42
00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:49.222
Luke's trial delayed their trip for a few days, so they were busier than ever.

43
00:02:49.242 --> 00:02:52.783
"You were incredible," Tommy said with awe.

44
00:02:52.803 --> 00:02:57.524
"No, Tommy, Bob was the one who saved Luke," the doctor corrected.

45
00:02:57.948 --> 00:02:59.810
"He was very loyal and brave."

46
00:03:01.771 --> 00:03:05.234
A man wearing clean clothes and a big smile walked up to them.

47
00:03:05.254 --> 00:03:06.795
"Dr. Dolittle?"

48
00:03:07.216 --> 00:03:07.896
he called out.

49
00:03:08.637 --> 00:03:10.398
Tommy could not believe his eyes.

50
00:03:10.939 --> 00:03:11.639
It was Luke!

51
00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.841
He looked completely different.

52
00:03:14.542 --> 00:03:15.362
Luke and Dr.

53
00:03:15.422 --> 00:03:17.164
Dolittle spoke for a few minutes.

54
00:03:19.366 --> 00:03:23.489
"I'm very sorry, but I won't be able to join you on your voyage," Luke said.

55
00:03:23.509 --> 00:03:26.732
"That's quite all right," replied the doctor.

56
00:03:27.468 --> 00:03:29.929
"But I do want to give you something," said Luke.

57
00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:32.331
Luke let out a loud whistle.

58
00:03:34.532 --> 00:03:37.954
Bob, Jip, and Sweetie arrived, pulling a large wagon.

59
00:03:40.035 --> 00:03:42.096
Dr. Dolittle uncovered the wagon.

60
00:03:42.756 --> 00:03:44.697
It was filled with all kinds of food.

61
00:03:44.717 --> 00:03:46.538
"Oh, Luke!

62
00:03:46.879 --> 00:03:48.660
Just what we need for our trip!"

63
00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.160
the doctor exclaimed.

64
00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:54.243
"Mendoza had to return my gold rock," Luke said shyly.

65
00:03:54.263 --> 00:03:56.644
"So now I have lots of money."

66
00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:02.343
Just then Polynesia came by with an unexpected visitor.

67
00:04:02.363 --> 00:04:04.105
"Dr. Dolittle!"

68
00:04:04.666 --> 00:04:05.386
she cried out.

69
00:04:05.406 --> 00:04:06.928
"Guess who I met?"

70
00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:09.570
Dr. Dolittle rubbed his eyes.

71
00:04:10.351 --> 00:04:12.252
He couldn't believe what he was seeing.

72
00:04:12.272 --> 00:04:15.075
"Is that the prince of Jolliginki?"

73
00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:16.036
he said.

74
00:04:17.918 --> 00:04:19.039
It was indeed.

75
00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:22.502
Years ago, the African prince had helped Dr.

76
00:04:22.542 --> 00:04:24.604
Dolittle escape from his father's prison.

77
00:04:25.476 --> 00:04:28.619
"I am a university student now," explained the prince.

78
00:04:29.179 --> 00:04:32.161
"When I heard you were living here, I had to come and see you."

79
00:04:32.181 --> 00:04:36.104
"Well, I'm so glad you did," said the doctor.

80
00:04:38.166 --> 00:04:40.508
They spoke awhile about the prince's family.

81
00:04:41.008 --> 00:04:44.531
Suddenly the doctor asked, "Would you like to travel with us?"

82
00:04:45.091 --> 00:04:48.634
The prince answered immediately, "I would be delighted!

83
00:04:49.094 --> 00:04:50.916
I am on my summer holidays at the moment."

84
00:04:52.996 --> 00:04:54.377
"That's wonderful!"

85
00:04:54.778 --> 00:04:55.638
the doctor said.

86
00:04:55.658 --> 00:04:58.140
"Now we're ready for our voyage!"

87
00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:03.985
"But, Doctor," interrupted Tommy, "we need three people to sail The Curlew.

88
00:05:04.726 --> 00:05:05.927
Who is the third man?"

89
00:05:06.687 --> 00:05:09.890
"You are, Tommy," said the doctor, and he winked.
